esh-tarball Firefox 157 DOM/screenshot/offline tests (2 passed, 1 skipped with a 120-second container budget); independent-process SQLite; dashboard/network/visual/storage fixtures; fresh npm consumers including exact Node 18.18 and 20.0; CacheFn consumers with Vitest 3/4; Python 3.10/3.12 source and installed-wheel tests (20 each), strict mypy, Ruff, and dependency audits. See `testfn/.conduct/target-readiness.md` for measured results and limits.

This remains a draft. Native Safari WebDriver requires the local Allow remote automation setting. Historical IndexedDB floors (Chrome 24/Firefox 16/Safari 10/Edge 12) still need exact-engine validation. A standalone ES5/native-IDB bundle now includes runtime polyfills and prefixed factory support; Chrome and WebKit pass both normal and stripped-global fallback fixtures. Cleanup queues requests from IndexedDB callbacks so task-based Promise scheduling does not prematurely close transactions. The specification is preserved. Local fixture measurements do not establish universal speedup or deployment/SLA goals, and hosted CI has not been claimed as passed.


Framework subprocess ownership now continues until the owned POSIX process group disappears. Normal leader exits with surviving descendants are failures; cancellation, timeout and output overflow stop/escalate the group and await termination. Unconfirmed termination rejects instead of reporting that work stopped. Actual resistant-descendant tests cover ignored/closed stdio and preserve an unrelated sentinel. This increment passes55 core tests, types/build,14 final focused tests and9 actual-framework assertions. Evidence is included under .conduct; no shared packages or ignore rules changed. Windows process trees, escaped sessions and durable crash reconciliation remain open.

"}

